  "id": "hip-adduction",
  "name": "Hip Adduction",
  "definition": "A strict open-chain hip-adduction isolation. The roster owns the original unilateral supported standing band fixture and one exact bilateral Technogym seated isotonic-machine fixture at eighty degrees of hip flexion. Their support, start and endpoint, knee posture, resistance, path constraint, and cadence remain branch-specific. The visible adductor-longus and brevis region is primary, gracilis is secondary, and the trunk and pelvis roles remain categorical stabilizers. Other machines, cable, Copenhagen, squeeze, rotated, closed-chain, and multi-joint variants remain outside this contract.",
